### 1d. Intent Match Validation

**Searcher intent (one sentence):** Someone considering moving to or renting in Philadelphia wants to understand which neighborhoods match their lifestyle, budget, and commute needs so they can narrow their search.

**Primary intent:** Informational/navigational (discovery phase). The searcher is not yet ready to sign a lease. They are building a mental shortlist of neighborhoods.

**Secondary intent:** Comparison. They want neighborhoods contrasted against each other so they can self-select.

The **listicle with persona-based curation framing** matches this intent exactly. The article should help the reader self-identify ("this sounds like me") rather than imposing a universal ranking.

