## 3. Target Audience & Searcher Profile

The primary searcher is someone planning a move to Philadelphia: a young professional relocating from another city (frequently from New York, DC, or Boston), a graduate student choosing between University City and Center City options, or a first-time renter in their mid-20s trying to distinguish between Fishtown and Northern Liberties. They are in the **discovery and comparison phase** of the renter journey, building a shortlist before they start touring apartments. Their core problem is that Philadelphia has dozens of distinct neighborhoods and they lack the local knowledge to evaluate them quickly. They expect a structured format that lets them self-identify with a type (active lifestyle, foodie, transit-dependent, budget-conscious) and map that to specific neighborhood options.

